/-!
# Source recognition of the simple and triple M₂₂ modules

For the actual finite SQTK actor, with quasisimple F*(G), a faithful binary
action irreducible on that component, and cubic ratio at most two, the module
is the native degree-ten code or cocode, or the degree-twelve triple-cover
module. Each branch gives a marked ambient embedding and a whole-action
equivalence. The triple branch retains its four-element scalar coordinates
and the Frobenius action of outer elements.

The source degree and ambient-extension premises are discharged. The exact
Chapter K catalogue adapter is `M22Source.catalogue_markedModels`. Local
geometry and ratio calculations remain with their separate source owners.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, Chapter K, printed pp.451 and 457, and H.12–13.
-/
